// Adder.fol — package source file
// Spec: language-ref.md > Other ways to declare closures/function objects and
//       types/curried functions
//
// The second function-object binding form. Instead of an inline body, this
// binds an EXISTING callable by name:
//
//     add (a co.lang.int, b co.lang.int)->(co.lang.int) { this.return a + b; }
//     oObj co.lang.function = add;
//
// The two bindings terminate differently (DECISION-SYN-006):
//
//     inline anonymous body  ->  ends at `}`, no semicolon
//     expression binding     ->  ends at `;`
//
// Here the target is Basics.withDefaults, an ordinary unit function.

_ co.lang.function = Basics.withDefaults;
